# Deployment and Setup Guide

This guide details how to set up, run, and deploy the LangOctopus MCP application.

## Local Setup

### Prerequisites
- Python 3.8+
- Node.js 14+
- npm or yarn

### Environment Setup
- [env.example](mdc:env.example) - Example environment variables file that should be copied to `.env`
- [requirements.txt](mdc:requirements.txt) - Python dependencies

## Running the Application

- [run_ui.sh](mdc:run_ui.sh) - Script to run both frontend and backend servers
  - Checks if required ports (3001, 5001) are available
  - Installs dependencies if needed
  - Starts the Flask backend server
  - Starts the React frontend server

- [run.py](mdc:run.py) - Main runner script for the application

## AWS Lambda Deployment

The application can be deployed to AWS Lambda:

- [lambda/](mdc:lambda/) directory contains AWS Lambda specific code
- [.aws-sam/](mdc:.aws-sam/) directory contains AWS SAM deployment templates
- [lambda_client.py](mdc:lambda_client.py) - Client for interacting with Lambda functions
- [lambda_client_adapter.py](mdc:lambda_client_adapter.py) - Adapter for the Lambda client

## Testing

- [run_tests.py](mdc:run_tests.py) - Script to run tests
- [test_queries.py](mdc:test_queries.py) - Sample test queries

## Configuration

- [config/](mdc:config/) directory contains configuration files for different environments
